{"data": [{"author_id": "2896373517", "created_at": "2026-10-24T21:18:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114104301245059296"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/dvO0YDdM0a", "end": 252, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/luellamech/status/2114104301245059296/video/1", "media_key": "13_2114104128301420545", "start": 229, "url": "https://t.co/dvO0YDdM0a"}, {"display_url": "x.com/rimtoln/status…", "end": 276, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/rimtoln/status/2113037027499208964", "start": 253, "url": "https://t.co/2lN4tacQbu"}]}, "id": "2114104301245059296", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 1532, "like_count": 55, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113037027499208964", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "MUSK WANTS 440,000 NVIDIA VERA RUBIN SYSTEMS ONLINE BY Q2. FANTASTIC NEWS FOR NVIDIA INVESTORS?\nBUYS, BUILDS, RENTS OUT.\n\nEvery chip story says trust me.\nThis one comes with a quarterly report you can check. Here's what's in it: https://t.co/dvO0YDdM0a https://t.co/2lN4tacQbu", "url": "https://x.com/luellamech/status/2114104301245059296"}, {"author_id": "1429725410003062785", "created_at": "2026-10-24T21:59:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114114594058707002"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/2XnYVV5cE3", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/0xkydo/status/2114114594058707002/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114113909359562752", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/2XnYVV5cE3"}]}, "id": "2114114594058707002", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 258, "impression_count": 77584, "like_count": 721, "quote_count": 10, "reply_count": 39, "retweet_count": 44}, "text": "I don’t think folks realize just how insane DeepInfer is.\n\nOne cluster with DeepInfer. IN One day. Can produce AS MUCH tokens AS OpenRouter in an entire week.\n\n“A single cluster currently serves 155 trillion tokens per day, with overall revenue of US$38 per GPU-hour (at valley https://t.co/2XnYVV5cE3", "url": "https://x.com/0xkydo/status/2114114594058707002"}, {"author_id": "15091755", "created_at": "2026-10-24T23:13:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114133316031119616"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/bonegpt/status…", "end": 182, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/bonegpt/status/2114035719853265264", "start": 159, "url": "https://t.co/OyztjkKwGg"}]}, "id": "2114133316031119616", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 13, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114035719853265264", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Loose TOS is a marketing strategy. I will expect to see Torrent/Tor style LLM connections where your local GPU is a slice of a larger anonymous based cluster. https://t.co/OyztjkKwGg", "url": "https://x.com/williamsbk/status/2114133316031119616"}, {"author_id": "1730969855783018496", "created_at": "2026-10-24T23:15:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114133706617352610"], "id": "2114133706617352610", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 88, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "calling Dario Amodei to feel better about AI safety is wild. Bill Gates picked the one guy in tech who will gladly give you an existential panic attack about a GPU cluster", "url": "https://x.com/shadowaguy/status/2114133706617352610"}, {"author_id": "1664377198340366427", "created_at": "2026-10-25T01:38:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114169600875131274"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/pequityresearc…", "end": 191, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/pequityresearch/status/2114129419879014751", "start": 168, "url": "https://t.co/gsN0g9QoAd"}]}, "id": "2114169600875131274", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114129419879014751", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "The on-site generation point is the interesting one. Ran the numbers on a GPU cluster last year and grid price dominated the unit economics more than the hardware did. https://t.co/gsN0g9QoAd", "url": "https://x.com/ventureeat/status/2114169600875131274"}, {"author_id": "2065170645059846144", "created_at": "2026-10-25T00:06:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114146649559949719"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/AIonBase_/stat…", "end": 195, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/AIonBase_/status/2113262654605427069", "start": 172, "url": "https://t.co/lfxPxpCG4f"}]}, "id": "2114146649559949719", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1175, "like_count": 10, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113262654605427069", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Our bet: most AI activity on Base ends up being agents paying for their own inference, GPU jobs and data, with no human topping up an API key. \n\nCluster is built for that. https://t.co/lfxPxpCG4f", "url": "https://x.com/OpenProtocolFND/status/2114146649559949719"}, {"author_id": "849661480869912576", "created_at": "2026-10-25T00:10:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114147581593079990"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 16, "start": 11, "tag": "MSFT"}]}, "id": "2114147581593079990", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 299, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Microsoft ($MSFT) is projected by analysts to expand capital expenditures to approximately $210bn in FY27, stepping up from a $175bn outlook for CY26 to support continuous datacenter capacity additions of at least 1 GW per quarter. For F1Q27, total capital expenditures including", "url": "https://x.com/OptionKing666/status/2114147581593079990"}, {"article": {"title": "OpenAI Dates the Pause, Cuts the Cable"}, "author_id": "8071902", "created_at": "2026-10-25T00:17:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114149404361863610"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/i/article/2114…", "end": 244, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2114148343089614850", "start": 221, "status": 404, "unwound_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2114148343089614850", "url": "https://t.co/2nOIcixsBp"}]}, "id": "2114149404361863610", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 1467, "like_count": 11, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 11, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "OpenAI finally put dates on its training pause and cut the live internet for good. Two of Claude Code’s public faces signed off. Also: twelve years of replicated SQLite, and Sweden’s government blocks ChatGPT and Claude. https://t.co/2nOIcixsBp", "url": "https://x.com/zaibatsu/status/2114149404361863610"}, {"author_id": "1600530338920415232", "created_at": "2026-10-25T01:45:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114171378299527537"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/elonmusk/statu…", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/elonmusk/status/2114168277882581486", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/bXDBggTSj2"}]}, "id": "2114171378299527537", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 373, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114168277882581486", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "The financial mechanism of \"Stranded Compute\":\n\nCutting-edge AI silicon (GB200/GB300) depreciates aggressively at ~2.5% to 3.0% per month over a 36-48 month economic life. \n\nWhen a 50MW cluster sits unenergized for 6 to 9 months waiting on delayed 115kV substations or secondary https://t.co/bXDBggTSj2", "url": "https://x.com/LiDaosen/status/2114171378299527537"}, {"author_id": "1127775925058166784", "created_at": "2026-10-24T23:31:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114137773963690102"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/wyEFg6W6Bc", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/DamiBenveniste/status/2114137773963690102/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114137772025921536", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/wyEFg6W6Bc"}]}, "id": "2114137773963690102", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 91, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Before using GPUDirect Storage for image training, check where your JPEGs are decoded.\n\nWith a supported GPU and I/O stack, bytes can reach GPU memory without CPU staging. CPU JPEG decoding still needs CPU data. The direct path requires separate I/O integration and GPU-side https://t.co/wyEFg6W6Bc", "url": "https://x.com/DamiBenveniste/status/2114137773963690102"}, {"author_id": "85244302", "created_at": "2026-10-24T23:14:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114133391419294143"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/dlQkNpvd9D", "end": 300, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/RizeOnline/status/2114133391419294143/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114133354089963520", "start": 277, "url": "https://t.co/dlQkNpvd9D"}]}, "id": "2114133391419294143", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 56, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Meet Dolphin 2.8 Mistral 7B v02 — a mature 7B local model for predictable, private conversations, coding, and prompt experiments.\n\n🧭 Overview\nDolphin 2.8 is built on the Mistral 7B v0.2 family. The model card describes a 32K context window and full-weight fine-tuning with 16K https://t.co/dlQkNpvd9D", "url": "https://x.com/RizeOnline/status/2114133391419294143"}, {"author_id": "299947622", "created_at": "2026-10-24T22:36:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114123860417372634"], "id": "2114123860417372634", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 108, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Prediction: within 18 months, at least one major GPU cloud will report agent-execution as a bigger revenue line than model training rental.\n\nThe $300M sandbox line item is the early signal. Training was the first era, chat the second. The meter is already moving.", "url": "https://x.com/iamericpereira/status/2114123860417372634"}, {"author_id": "2108921330548482048", "created_at": "2026-10-24T21:25:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114105970020253814"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 243, "start": 240, "tag": "AI"}], "urls": [{"description": "AWS makes SageMaker AI training sessions generally available: write the model customization loop in Python while the service manages the GPUs.", "display_url": "jumpdaily.news/modelos-y-chip…", "end": 267, "expanded_url": "https://jumpdaily.news/modelos-y-chips/amazon-sagemaker-ai-opens-training-sessions-no-gpu/", "images": [{"height": 1067, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114105982347354112/cSgY7Icz?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1600}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114105982347354112/cSgY7Icz?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 244, "status": 200, "title": "SageMaker AI training sessions: GPUs managed by AWS", "unwound_url": "https://jumpdaily.news/modelos-y-chips/amazon-sagemaker-ai-opens-training-sessions-no-gpu/", "url": "https://t.co/b76sfbFCxa"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/mrQH2uQV4O", "end": 291, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/jumpdaily_EN/status/2114105970020253814/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114105968032100352", "start": 268, "url": "https://t.co/mrQH2uQV4O"}]}, "id": "2114105970020253814", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "BREAKING | Amazon SageMaker AI opens training sessions with no GPU management\n\nWhy it matters to you: Those who train models on AWS can write their own training loop without managing the GPUs, with token-based billing according to NeoTeo.\n\n#AI\nhttps://t.co/b76sfbFCxa https://t.co/mrQH2uQV4O", "url": "https://x.com/jumpdaily_EN/status/2114105970020253814"}, {"author_id": "2091433996467269633", "created_at": "2026-10-25T01:23:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114165850144120917"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "Vcity.ai", "end": 23, "expanded_url": "https://Vcity.ai", "start": 0, "status": 200, "title": "vcity.ai", "unwound_url": "https://Vcity.ai", "url": "https://t.co/mlLqLAxfYu"}, {"display_url": "x.com/SatoVorn/statu…", "end": 261, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/SatoVorn/status/2113949604190261350", "start": 238, "url": "https://t.co/uNy6fnJhd8"}]}, "id": "2114165850144120917", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 29, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113949604190261350", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "https://t.co/mlLqLAxfYu focuses on coordinating GPU resources for AI training and inference, with workload allocation and verifiable execution.\n\nThe real challenge is turning distributed computing power into coordinated, usable capacity. https://t.co/uNy6fnJhd8", "url": "https://x.com/Yangziemn/status/2114165850144120917"}, {"author_id": "2078707395438759936", "created_at": "2026-10-24T22:02:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114115312023162912"], "id": "2114115312023162912", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 14, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Tenstorrent just raised $1.5B at a $6.2B valuation — more than double its late-2024 mark. The bet: inference for open-weight models, not another training GPU. 🧵", "url": "https://x.com/sunder0yct/status/2114115312023162912"}, {"author_id": "23267952", "created_at": "2026-10-24T21:56:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114113770662277126"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Unlock FP/BF16 instruction issue rate on Nvidia 3000's cards to their professional equivalents - Zagitta/gpu-unlock", "display_url": "github.com/Zagitta/gpu-un…", "end": 221, "expanded_url": "https://github.com/Zagitta/gpu-unlock", "images": [{"height": 600, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114593688383098880/Av3QSu-k?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114593688383098880/Av3QSu-k?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 198, "status": 200, "title": "GitHub - Zagitta/gpu-unlock: Unlock FP/BF16 instruction issue rate on Nvidia 3000's cards to their professional equivalents", "unwound_url": "https://github.com/Zagitta/gpu-unlock", "url": "https://t.co/d9OybEvp1l"}]}, "id": "2114113770662277126", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 312, "like_count": 7, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Tried gpu-unlock on my RTX 3060 12GB.\n\nBF16 matmul: 48.1 TFLOPS measured vs ~25 stock spec\nTF32: 23.6 vs ~12.7\n\nOn paper that puts it between a stock 3070 Ti and a 3080 for ML training, on a 3060.\n\nhttps://t.co/d9OybEvp1l", "url": "https://x.com/souuzaa/status/2114113770662277126"}, {"author_id": "1263755555463507968", "created_at": "2026-10-25T01:37:44.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114169505610186863"], "id": "2114169505610186863", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 16, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Training a humanoid used to mean a server room.\n\nNow one GPU + a few hours can beat a week on 128.\n\nWhen compute stops being the gate, investors should ask a colder question: who owns the motion data, and who owns distribution into the real world?", "url": "https://x.com/SMTH6666/status/2114169505610186863"}, {"author_id": "1612087356533923841", "created_at": "2026-10-25T00:11:48.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114147879421952064"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 84, "start": 79, "tag": "DATA"}, {"end": 148, "start": 143, "tag": "CHIP"}, {"end": 195, "start": 189, "tag": "PEARL"}], "hashtags": [{"end": 248, "start": 241, "tag": "Crypto"}, {"end": 252, "start": 249, "tag": "AI"}], "urls": [{"description": "Non-dilutive GPU loans for GPU cloud operators, and GPU-backed credit for institutional capital, scored on one standard.", "display_url": "USD.AI", "end": 141, "expanded_url": "https://USD.AI", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2112517185956392960/eSwQ59Qh?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2112517185956392960/eSwQ59Qh?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 118, "status": 200, "title": "Capital markets for compute | USD.AI", "unwound_url": "https://USD.AI", "url": "https://t.co/LnhjSOfnxP"}]}, "id": "2114147879421952064", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "🚨 Grayscale named 3 cryptos that could benefit from the AI boom: DATA Network ($DATA) for licensing AI training data, https://t.co/LnhjSOfnxP ($CHIP) for financing GPU hardware, and Pearl ($PEARL) for merging proof-of-work with AI compute 🤖 #Crypto #AI", "url": "https://x.com/Cryptohods/status/2114147879421952064"}, {"author_id": "1224918819195498496", "created_at": "2026-10-25T00:29:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114152318895554961"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 12, "id": "1881421472981303296", "start": 0, "username": "quipnetwork"}]}, "id": "2114152318895554961", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@Quipnetwork is shaking up AI compute. It's a decentralized platform connecting idle GPUs for affordable model training &amp; deployment.\n\nHow? By leveraging blockchain tech to create a marketplace for GPU resources. Users can tap into this power for AI projects.", "url": "https://x.com/Idrisrabiu360/status/2114152318895554961"}, {"author_id": "1366093717678026753", "created_at": "2026-10-24T21:22:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114105205700669636"]